For the first 60 seconds, the voice loops were literally chaotic

102
00:08:12,581 --> 00:08:17,640
because so many reports were coming in as the controllers would see jets firing

103
00:08:17,641 --> 00:08:21,320
and they'd see the electrical problem progress through other elements of the system.

104
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:28,280
On board Apollo 13, there is a loss of power in what is called Main Bus B,

105
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:31,620
one of two main power distribution panels.

106
00:08:31,621 --> 00:08:38,180
If one is gone, it means that half the systems in the spacecraft are dead.

107
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:43,780
As in all space travel, adequate electrical power is critical.

108
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:48,720
Without it, all vital systems aboard Apollo 13 would go dark,

109
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:52,360
transforming the most advanced spacecraft in the world

110
00:08:52,361 --> 00:08:56,060
into a metal hulk aimlessly drifting in space

111
00:08:56,061 --> 00:08:58,900
without navigation or life support systems.

112
00:08:58,901 --> 00:09:05,900
I knew it was something very serious, something not normal, very wrong, because there were

113
00:09:05,901 --> 00:09:09,900
a very large number of caution and warning lights on.

114
00:09:09,901 --> 00:09:12,900
The caution warning light array has two color lights.

115
00:09:12,901 --> 00:09:18,900
Some are red, which generally means very bad, and some are orange or yellow, which means

116
00:09:18,901 --> 00:09:20,900
