124
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:11,900
In the meantime, Jack Swigert is called mission control.

125
00:10:11,901 --> 00:10:14,900
Houston, we've had a problem here.

126
00:10:14,901 --> 00:10:17,900
Can I say again, please?

127
00:10:17,901 --> 00:10:20,900
Houston, we've had a problem.

128
00:10:20,901 --> 00:10:26,640
You get that sort of burning sensation in the stomach, and you say, why me? Why now?

129
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,180
Why didn't it happen on 12 or wait to 14?

130
00:10:29,181 --> 00:10:31,340
And what do we do to get out of this thing?

131
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:38,380
Then it dawned on me that we are in more serious trouble than merely not landing on the moon.

132
00:10:38,381 --> 00:10:44,120
And that's when our thought process changed from being one of disappointment to one of survival.

133
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:49,980
Relying on his pilot's instincts, Commander Lovell eyeballs the situation.

134
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,900
He looks out the window and doesn't like what he sees.

135
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:58,320
