190
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:42,720
And we have a

191
00:15:42,721 --> 00:15:46,700
procedure for getting power from the lamp.

192
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:50,720
We'd like you to copy down. Okay. Stand by, Jack.

193
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:54,960
That sounds like good news. I made a call to the crew and I said,

194
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:58,860
look, flight controllers, settle down. Let's make your calls crisp. Electrical

195
00:15:58,861 --> 00:16:02,248
bus A is still good. Don't do anything to screw it up. The lunar module's attached.

196
00:16:02,249 --> 00:16:02,949
We're going to

197
00:16:02,950 --> 00:16:04,133
use that as our lifeboat.

198
00:16:04,134 --> 00:16:07,440
Get me more people, get me more communications, and get me more

199
00:16:07,441 --> 00:16:13,260
computing capabilities. And this was what I would say the turning point in the fight

200
00:16:13,261 --> 00:16:14,713
to save the crew.

201
00:16:14,714 --> 00:16:20,440
The concept of using the lunar module as a lifeboat was explored on

202
00:16:20,441 --> 00:16:23,389
earlier missions and run in simulations.

203
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:26,780
The operations team envisioned using the lunar

