219
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:38,980
And that was going to be difficult

220
00:17:38,981 --> 00:17:44,520
because the explosion had created yet another problem for Apollo 13.

221
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:50,520
When I looked out the window, the explosion had put around the spacecraft

222
00:17:50,521 --> 00:17:52,480
thousands of small pieces of debris,

223
00:17:52,481 --> 00:17:56,720
And these were false stars. We couldn't tell a real star from a false star.

224
00:17:57,100 --> 00:18:03,580
There was no way to do a star sighting to know whether our platform had been aligned correctly or not.

225
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:08,160
We're moving seven miles a second toward the moon.

226
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:14,020
And this debris cloud actually is moving along with us.

227
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:20,720
And until we perform a maneuver to get away from that debris, it's going to be with us.

